# 📚 Stacks & Queues (Part 3) - Introduction to Queue

## 📌 Introduction

A **Queue** is a linear data structure that follows the **FIFO (First In, First Out)** principle.

This means the **first element inserted is the first one to be removed.**

Think of people standing in a queue at a ticket counter:

- The first person to join the line gets served first.
- New people always join at the end.

Queues are widely used in operating systems, networking, scheduling algorithms, and graph traversal.

